<div class="vgpu-panel">
<h3><i class="fa fa-plug"></i> VF Passthrough</h3>
<p>VFs are automatically bound to <code class="vgpu-mono">vfio-pci</code> so you can add them to VMs.
<b>Never passthrough the PF (<?= htmlspecialchars($intel_pf ?: '00:02.0') ?>)</b> - it would crash all other VFs.</p>
<table class="vgpu-table">
<tr><th>PCI</th><th>Driver</th></tr>
<?php
$vf_list = [];
if ($intel_pf) {
  $out = shell_exec("lspci -D 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'VGA compatible controller|Display controller' | grep -i intel | awk '{print \$1}' | grep -v '\\.0' | sort");
  foreach (preg_split('/\s+/', trim($out)) as $vf) {
    if ($vf === '') continue;
    $drv = @readlink("/sys/bus/pci/devices/$vf/driver");
    $drv = $drv ? basename($drv) : 'none';
    $vf_list[] = [$vf, $drv];
  }
}
?>
<?php if (!$vf_list): ?>
<tr><td colspan="2"><i>No VFs currently created - set the VF count above.</i></td></tr>
<?php else: foreach ($vf_list as $v): ?>
<tr><td><?= htmlspecialchars($v[0]) ?></td>
    <td><?= $v[1] === 'vfio-pci' ? "<span class='vgpu-ok'>vfio-pci</span>" : htmlspecialchars($v[1]) ?></td></tr>
<?php endforeach; endif; ?>
</table>
</div>

<div class="vgpu-panel">
<h3><i class="fa fa-terminal"></i> Boot Parameters</h3>
<p>The following parameters must be on the syslinux append line (Settings -&gt; Boot) for SR-IOV to
survive a reboot. The plugin does not modify syslinux automatically; add them manually:</p>
<pre class="vgpu-mono" style="background:rgba(0,0,0,.25);padding:10px;border-radius:4px">intel_iommu=on i915.enable_guc=3 i915.max_vfs=<?= htmlspecialchars($vfnum) ?> module_blacklist=xe</pre>
<p style="opacity:.7">Also make sure <code class="vgpu-mono">/boot/config/modprobe.d/i915.conf</code> blacklists the
<code class="vgpu-mono">xe</code> driver so i915 owns the GPU.</p>
</div>

